2026-03-25 17:07:08 - Agent_20260325170345 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 5 CodeQL queries covering path traversal vulnerabilities in Spring Cloud Config Server. Key findings:

1. AbstractScmAccessor.java:266 - File constructor receives user-controlled path from HTTP parameters (application/profile/label) via template substitution in getSearchLocations(), no path canonicalization before filesystem operation.

2. NativeEnvironmentRepository.java:230 - startsWith() containment check BEFORE cleanPath() normalization - check-then-normalize anti-pattern that can be bypassed with paths like /base/../../../etc/passwd.

3. NativeEnvironmentRepository.java:242 - Same check-before-normalize anti-pattern at a different startsWith() call site.

4. NativeEnvironmentRepository.java:252 - Third instance of check-before-normalize pattern.

5. SvnKitEnvironmentRepository.java:191 - User-controlled path data flows to SVN resource loading operations without adequate path validation.

Total 6 findings submitted (5 true positives covering the distinct vulnerable locations, with some duplicates for the SVN findings).
